hadiths[4]{hadithnumber,text}:
"15530","Hushaym narrated to us: Abu Balj informed us, from Muhammad ibn Hatib al-Jumahi, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The distinction between the lawful and the unlawful is the duff and the voice in marriage."
"15531","Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, from Shubah, from Simak, he said: Muhammad ibn Hatib said: Something poured upon my hand from a pot, so my mother took me to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was in a place, he said: So he said speech in which was: Remove the harm, Lord of mankind, and I think he said: Heal, You are the Healer, he said: And he used to spit."
"15532","Ibrahim ibn Abi al-Abbas and Yunus ibn Muhammad both said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Uthman narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn al-Abbas said in his hadith: Ibn Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Hatib, he said: My father narrated to me, from his grandfather Muhammad ibn Hatib, from his mother Umm Jamil bint al-Mujallil, she said: I came with you from the land of Abyssinia, until when I was a night or two nights from Madinah, I cooked for you a cooked dish, and the firewood ran out, so I went out seeking it, and you reached for the pot and it overturned upon your forearm. So I brought you to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: May my father and mother be ransom for you, O Messenger of Allah, this is Muhammad ibn Hatib. So he spat in your mouth and wiped over your head and supplicated for you, and began spitting upon your hands and saying: Remove the harm, Lord of mankind, and heal, You are the Healer, there is no healing except Your healing, a healing that leaves no sickness. She said: So I did not get up with you from with him until your hand had healed."
"15533","Ibrahim ibn Abi al-Abbas narrated to us, he said: Sharik narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, from Muhammad ibn Hatib, he said: I crawled to a pot while it was boiling, and I put my hand in it, and it burned, or he said: my hand swelled. So my mother took me to a man who was at al-Batha, and he said something and blew. Then when it was in the rule of Uthman, I said to my mother: Who was that man? She said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
